steps.body:
You can throw exceptions yourself. The idiom is to validate arguments at the top of a method and throw before changing anything, so a failed call leaves the object as it was:

```java
public void setSeat(int seat) {
    if (seat < 1 || seat > 50) {
        throw new IllegalArgumentException("Seat must be 1 to 50, got " + seat);
    }
    this.seat = seat;
}
```

`throw` ends the method at once, like `return`, and the exception travels up to the nearest caller with a matching `catch`. If no method catches it, the program crashes. Pick the type that says what went wrong:

- `IllegalArgumentException`: the caller passed a bad value.
- `IllegalStateException`: the value is fine, but the object is in the wrong state for this call, such as using a ticket twice.

The method throws, and the caller decides what to do. Here `main` catches and prints the message, then moves on to the next command.

Gotcha: `NumberFormatException` is a subclass of `IllegalArgumentException`, so `catch (IllegalArgumentException e)` also catches a failed `parseInt`.

example.code:
import java.io.BufferedReader;
import java.io.IOException;
import java.io.InputStreamReader;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {
        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));
        Ticket ticket = new Ticket();
        String line;
        while ((line = br.readLine()) != null) {
            if (line.isBlank()) {
                continue;
            }
            String[] parts = line.strip().split("\\s+");
            try {
                switch (parts[0]) {
                    case "seat" -> {
                        ticket.setSeat(Integer.parseInt(parts[1]));
                        System.out.println("Seat " + ticket.getSeat() + " booked");
                    }
                    case "use" -> {
                        ticket.use();
                        System.out.println("Entered with seat " + ticket.getSeat());
                    }
                    default -> System.out.println("Unknown command: " + parts[0]);
                }
            } catch (IllegalArgumentException e) {
                System.out.println("Invalid: " + e.getMessage());
            } catch (IllegalStateException e) {
                System.out.println("Refused: " + e.getMessage());
            }
        }
    }
}

class Ticket {
    private int seat;
    private boolean used;

    public void setSeat(int seat) {
        if (seat < 1 || seat > 50) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Seat must be 1 to 50, got " + seat);
        }
        this.seat = seat;
    }

    public void use() {
        if (seat == 0) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("No seat chosen");
        }
        if (used) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Ticket already used");
        }
        used = true;
    }

    public int getSeat() {
        return seat;
    }
}

